# Intrusion Detection & Security Monitoring System

## Overview

This project is a Spring Boot application for monitoring and responding to suspicious access patterns. It includes user registration, JWT-based authentication, security event logging, detection rules, and brute-force alerting.

The system is designed to:

- register and manage users
- authenticate users with JWT
- record failed and successful login events
- evaluate detection rules such as brute-force attempts
- create and resolve security alerts
- persist data in PostgreSQL

---

## Features

- User registration and retrieval
- Login endpoint with JWT token generation
- Security event tracking
- Brute-force detection using threshold-based rules
- Alert creation and resolution flow
- Dockerized PostgreSQL deployment

---

## Project Structure

```text
.
├── src/
│   ├── main/
│   │   ├── java/
│   │   └── resources/
│   └── test/
├── Dockerfile
├── docker-compose.yml
├── pom.xml
├── mvnw
├── readme
└── HELP.md
```

Main application files:

- [docker-compose.yml](docker-compose.yml) — PostgreSQL + app container setup
- [src/main/resources/application.properties](src/main/resources/application.properties) — datasource and config
- [src/main/java/com/cloud/ids/config/SecurityConfig.java](src/main/java/com/cloud/ids/config/SecurityConfig.java) — endpoint security rules
- [src/main/java/com/cloud/ids/service/DetectionRuleService.java](src/main/java/com/cloud/ids/service/DetectionRuleService.java) — default brute-force rule setup

